WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:05.590
2017 has already seen some great video game
releases, with hits like The Legend of Zelda:

00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:10.660
Breath of the Wild, Resident Evil 7, and Horizon:
Zero Dawn grabbing the headlines.

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:14.690
But while the mainstream gaming media has
been focused on picking apart every minor

00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:19.150
flaw in Mass Effect: Andromeda, there have
also been a ton of great smaller releases

00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:23.070
that have slipped through the cracks, overshadowed
by the big guns.

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:24.070
Until now.

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:27.460
Grab your controller and fire up your Twitch
stream, because here's a look at the best

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:30.869
games you've already missed in 2017.

00:00:30.869 --> 00:00:32.240
Night in the Woods

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:36.210
Infinite Fall's Night in the Woods is a deep
and stylish meandering through the little

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:40.920
things in life, with a healthy dose of musing
on the nature of God and the meaning of human

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:41.920
existence.

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:46.800
It also explores the boredom of working class
America while presenting an engaging mystery

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:50.480
and allowing players to explore mini-games
and side missions galore.

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:55.300
And the beautifully designed dream sequences,
filled with fear, emptiness, and the search

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:57.400
for meaning, are not to be missed.

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:10.280
Clocking in at 10 awesome free-to-play hours,
Night in the Woods is one game that shouldn't

00:01:10.289 --> 00:01:12.289
be missed.

00:01:12.289 --> 00:01:13.640
Statik

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:18.060
If you're looking for something a little different,
welcome to Statik, a puzzle-solving virtual

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:22.369
reality experience in which you don't know
where you are, who you're with, or why your

00:01:22.369 --> 00:01:25.710
hands are locked inside increasingly difficult
puzzle boxes.

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:30.119
The puzzles themselves strike just the right
balance between trickiness and ease, while

00:01:30.119 --> 00:01:34.119
the atmosphere in which you're tasked with
solving them is downright creepy.

00:01:34.119 --> 00:01:38.700
The first generation of virtual reality consoles
have been criticized for not having enough

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:44.530
killer games to justify the cost, but innovative
and fun experiences like Statik are quickly

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:46.270
changing that notion.

00:01:46.270 --> 00:01:47.580
Try it and see for yourself!

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:50.219
Wonder Boy: The Dragon's Trap

00:01:50.219 --> 00:01:55.200
Available for Switch and the PS4, Wonder Boy:
The Dragon's Trap is a perfect example of

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:58.649
how to make a 30-year-old game great in 2017.

00:01:58.649 --> 00:02:04.409
A remake of a 1989 game, Wonder Boy: The Dragon's
Trap has been revamped with a beautiful and

00:02:04.409 --> 00:02:09.600
cartoony art style, while retaining the original
platformer's story and mechanics.

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:14.230
As a bonus, players can even choose to play
the original version instead if they want,

00:02:14.230 --> 00:02:17.080
which is pretty much the ultimate in retro
gaming.

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:18.110
The Sexy Brutale

00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:23.390
Cursed to remain trapped in a never-ending
masquerade ball, players in The Sexy Brutale

00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:28.420
have to try to prevent a series of murders
which take place on a continual, time-bending

00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:29.420
loop.

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:33.510
To solve the mystery, players must master
the essence of the game's time-looping mechanic,

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:37.810
in addition to flexing their investigative
muscles in ways the classic board game Clue

00:02:37.810 --> 00:02:39.330
could only dream about.

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:44.120
The Sexy Brutale isn't very long, but after
you've solved the last murder, you'll be left

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:45.640
itching for more.

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:46.780
Hidden Folks

00:02:46.780 --> 00:02:51.510
Take one look at this game's artistic style
and it's impossible not to be intrigued.

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:56.530
Combining classic Where's Waldo style hunting
fun with gorgeous, hand-drawn visuals in a

00:02:56.530 --> 00:03:01.040
one-of-a-kind gameplay experience, Hidden
Folks is perfect for mobile phones while also

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:03.260
being right at home on PC and Mac.

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:08.050
The daydreamy landscapes are teeming with
activity, but as the title implies, much of

00:03:08.050 --> 00:03:12.060
it is hidden, inviting you to explore the
game to discover its many secrets.

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:17.160
Be warned, though: once you start playing,
it's nearly impossible to stop, so don't boot

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:20.590
up Hidden Folks unless you have a lot of free
time available.

00:03:20.590 --> 00:03:22.230
You're going to need it.

00:03:22.230 --> 00:03:23.230
TypeShift

00:03:23.230 --> 00:03:27.290
If you're sick of word jumbles, crosswords,
or sudoku, don't worry.

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:31.660
You just found your new daily obsession in
the form of TypeShift, which gives you columns

00:03:31.660 --> 00:03:36.260
of letters you have to arrange into words
until you've used up all of the letters available,

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:38.620
like a cross between Boggle and Tetris.

00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:40.710
It's simple, but deceptively difficult.

00:03:40.710 --> 00:03:42.430
Can you spell "addictive?"

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:46.260
Once you start playing Typeshift, you'll never
have to make eye contact with other people

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:49.340
on the bus ever again!

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:50.340
Candleman

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:54.280
With a unique combination of art direction
and gameplay, Candleman has already made a

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:58.990
name for itself as an innovative indie title
every curious gamer should try out.

00:03:58.990 --> 00:04:03.670
You play a candleman, who can only stay lit
for 10 seconds on his quest for a distant

00:04:03.670 --> 00:04:04.670
light.

00:04:04.670 --> 00:04:09.220
The game's mechanics and story play with the
contrast between darkness and illumination,

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:13.130
using the interaction to traverse a range
of obstacles and environments.

00:04:13.130 --> 00:04:17.680
Candleman is one of those little games that
sometimes gets overshadowed by bigger, louder,

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:19.459
more in your face titles.

00:04:19.459 --> 00:04:23.240
But this is one game that refuses to hide
its light under a bushel.

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:26.070
Fire up Candleman and let your gaming light
shine!

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:27.430
Hollow Knight

00:04:27.430 --> 00:04:31.290
If you ever wondered what Dark Souls would
look like if it were done Metroid style, then

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:33.320
Hollow Knight is the game for you.

00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:38.340
With incredible hand drawn graphics, breathtaking
music, and innovative sound effects, Hollow

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:42.780
Knight provides hours of entertainment as
you explore an environment filled with puzzles,

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:46.000
secret areas, and over 30 tough boss battles.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:50.570
For fans of side-scrolling adventure, it just
doesn't get any more stylish - or fun - than

00:04:50.570 --> 00:04:51.570
Hollow Knight.

00:04:51.570 --> 00:04:55.710
Plus, there are already whole communities
devoted to figuring out the game's rich and

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:56.910
mysterious lore.

00:04:56.910 --> 00:04:58.600
So what are you waiting for?

00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:01.900
Get out there and do… whatever it is you're
doing.

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:04.650
She Remembered Caterpillars

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:08.810
Featuring a hand-drawn art style reminiscent
of a children's book created under the influence

00:05:08.810 --> 00:05:13.630
of psychedelic mushrooms, this color based
puzzle game investigates the bond between

00:05:13.630 --> 00:05:17.210
parent and child in unexpected and strange
ways.

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:22.100
A mind-bending experience with a touch of
creepiness and more than a heap of weirdness,

00:05:22.100 --> 00:05:25.990
She Remembered Caterpillars is worth checking
out for anyone who is looking for something

00:05:25.990 --> 00:05:27.630
a little different.

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:28.630
Detention

00:05:28.630 --> 00:05:34.650
Set in 1960s Taiwan, Detention incorporates
elements of Taiwanese and Chinese culture

00:05:34.650 --> 00:05:39.940
and mythology into a disturbing experience
that PC Gamer said is, quote, "the closest

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:44.110
a game has come to capturing the essence of
the original Silent Hill games in years."

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:48.200
For most gamers, that should be about all
you need to know to give this one a shot.

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:54.010
But be warned: just like Silent Hill, Detention
is a creepy, and sometimes downright terrifying

00:05:54.010 --> 00:05:57.930
game that will haunt you long after you finally
set down the controller.

00:05:57.930 --> 00:06:10.320
You know what they say: In Taiwan, the game
finishes you.

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:11.590
Splitter Critters

00:06:11.590 --> 00:06:15.690
There's nothing quite as exciting as a game
that re-imagines gameplay itself.

00:06:15.690 --> 00:06:17.750
Splitter Critters does just that.

00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:21.720
The premise is simple: you're trying to help
critters find the exit to the level.

00:06:21.720 --> 00:06:24.020
But you don't actually control the critters.

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:27.950
Instead, with a swipe of your finger you can
tear the screen apart and then reposition

00:06:27.950 --> 00:06:30.240
the pieces to form a new level layout.

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:33.910
And since different types of critters have
different movement patterns, figuring out

00:06:33.910 --> 00:06:36.780
the best way to play god requires a lot of
strategy.

00:06:36.780 --> 00:06:37.840
Good luck.

00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:40.020
Because those critters are counting on you.

00:06:40.020 --> 00:06:41.440
Blaster Master Zero

00:06:41.440 --> 00:06:46.190
Taking players on a retro-trip to the golden
days of the Nintendo Entertainment System,

00:06:46.190 --> 00:06:50.780
Blaster Master Zero is an 8-bit side-scrolling
and top-down action-adventure game.

00:06:50.780 --> 00:06:55.800
Reinventing the classic 1988 title Blaster
Master, this new edition keeps all the fun

00:06:55.800 --> 00:07:00.490
of the original while updating gameplay with
three decades worth of innovation, making

00:07:00.490 --> 00:07:06.380
for a familiar yet fresh gameplay experience
that makes us giddy with nostalgic bliss.

00:07:06.380 --> 00:07:08.710
Torment: Tides of Numenera

00:07:08.710 --> 00:07:12.889
Most RPGs these days are heavy on the combat
and light on the narrative.

00:07:12.889 --> 00:07:18.220
Torment: Tides of Numenera goes the other
way, emphasizing story over collecting loot,

00:07:18.220 --> 00:07:23.040
resulting in a game that's closer to an interactive
fantasy novel than just another hack and slash

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:24.320
orc massacre.

00:07:24.320 --> 00:07:29.480
For old school RPG enthusiasts who love nearly
infinite dialogue trees, or for fans of the

00:07:29.480 --> 00:07:33.460
classic Choose Your Own Adventure novels,
Tides of Numenera is the game you've been

00:07:33.460 --> 00:07:35.030
waiting for.

00:07:35.030 --> 00:07:36.520
Robo Recall

00:07:36.520 --> 00:07:39.360
Afraid of an artificial-intelligence-filled
future?

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:41.210
Want to kill every robot you see?

00:07:41.210 --> 00:07:47.100
Oculus Rift owners, rejoice, because Robo
Recall is just the robot-slaying, first-person,

00:07:47.100 --> 00:07:50.130
virtual-reality experience you've been looking
for.

00:07:50.130 --> 00:07:54.340
One of the first games to really show the
potential of the Oculus Touch controllers,

00:07:54.340 --> 00:07:59.020
Robo Recall features optimized game play to
compliment beautiful art direction in one

00:07:59.020 --> 00:08:01.759
of the best shooting galleries ever devised.

00:08:01.759 --> 00:08:04.620
So give it a shot… no pun intended.

00:08:04.620 --> 00:08:06.009
Tales of Berseria

00:08:06.009 --> 00:08:12.440
Out in Japan since August of 2016, the acclaimed
RPG Tales of Berseria finally came westward

00:08:12.440 --> 00:08:13.860
in 2017.

00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:18.300
Despite praise from fans and critics alike,
though, Tales of Berseria has been heavily

00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:20.949
overshadowed by more hyped, triple-A games.

00:08:20.949 --> 00:08:22.680
Don't let that fool you, though.

00:08:22.680 --> 00:08:27.620
With an unusually dark and mature storyline,
and some truly memorable characters, Tales

00:08:27.620 --> 00:08:31.300
of Berseria features over 50 hours of engrossing
gameplay.

00:08:31.300 --> 00:08:35.399
Plus, it allows you to experience firsthand
what it might be like to live inside an anime

00:08:35.400 --> 00:08:36.240
world.

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:46.791
If there's one thing Japan knows how to do,
it's create incredible RPG adventures, so

00:08:46.791 --> 00:08:50.900
if you're a fan of the genre, or simply want
to find out what all the fuss is about, give

00:08:50.900 --> 00:08:52.710
Tales of Berseria a try.

00:08:52.710 --> 00:08:53.750
You won't regret it.

00:08:53.750 --> 00:08:55.050
Bleed 2

00:08:55.050 --> 00:08:59.770
There seems to be no shortage of retro-inspired
pixel-art games these days, but don't dismiss

00:08:59.770 --> 00:09:01.990
Bleed 2 as just another Contra clone.

00:09:01.990 --> 00:09:07.510
With buttery smooth controls, charming pixelated
animation, and boss battles that are truly

00:09:07.510 --> 00:09:12.310
epic, Bleed 2 manages to be accessible to
everyone while still rewarding those who wish

00:09:12.310 --> 00:09:14.870
to dive deeper into its intricacies.

00:09:14.870 --> 00:09:19.910
It's also more forgiving than most Contra-inspired
games, particularly on lower difficulty levels,

00:09:19.910 --> 00:09:24.670
and can be completed in roughly two hours,
so you really have no excuse not to give this

00:09:24.670 --> 00:09:26.020
one a shot.

00:09:26.020 --> 00:09:29.360
Pinball FX2: Star Wars Pinball - Rogue One

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:31.270
Pinball fans will enjoy this game.

00:09:31.270 --> 00:09:33.880
Fans of Star Wars: Rogue One will enjoy this
game.

00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:37.790
Heck, everyone who enjoys fun will like Star
Wars Pinball: Rogue One.

00:09:37.790 --> 00:09:42.660
It features tight mechanics, silky smooth
gameplay, and fantastic physics—with sound

00:09:42.660 --> 00:09:44.740
effects and movie quotes galore.

00:09:44.740 --> 00:09:49.180
Even casual fans of the film will appreciate
the level of detail and creativity that has

00:09:49.180 --> 00:09:53.980
gone into this table, whether it be the black
Deathtrooper firing lasers all over the place

00:09:53.980 --> 00:09:58.200
during a multiball, or Jyn giving the smackdown
to a stormtrooper.

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:00.890
So are you a pinball wizard - or a pinball
Jedi?

00:10:00.890 --> 00:10:03.670
Put your virtual quarter in and find out.

00:10:03.670 --> 00:10:04.950
Thimbleweed Park

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:10.170
If you like your adventures to be of the point-and-click
variety, look no further than the surefire

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:12.430
under-the-radar hit Thimbleweed Park.

00:10:12.430 --> 00:10:15.100
It's not just a point-and-click adventure
game, mind you.

00:10:15.100 --> 00:10:19.420
According to Polygon developer Whitney Reynolds,
it's actually "a point-and-click adventure

00:10:19.420 --> 00:10:24.620
game about point-and-click adventure games,"
with meta references to spiritual predecessors

00:10:24.620 --> 00:10:26.620
like Maniac Mansion.

00:10:26.620 --> 00:10:30.630
Fans of the genre would have to be true maniacs
to not give this one a go.

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:32.380
Just don't play it if you're easily offended.

00:10:42.340 --> 00:10:43.620
Thanks for watching!

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:46.680
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:10:46.680 --> 00:10:49.200
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

